  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> are angles of a triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the lengths of the sides opposite these angles are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math> respectively, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NQEnI",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> are in A.P.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OwwF3",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> are in A.P.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Gyjla",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "J01sO",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> are in A.P.",
